[b]Rim-MCP[/b] lets you connect your colony to your favourite MCP-supporting AI agent.

[i]For the modern high-impact 10x engineer looking to utilize agentic AI to drive business value in their colony.[/i]

[list]
[*]Ask deep questions about your stockpiles, pawns, recipes, and loaded content (including mods!).
[*]Dictate your schedule and work priorities through a client with voice support and have an agent apply them.
[*]Have the latest & greatest LLM pick your pawns' apparel policies.
[*]Many more possibilities!
[/list]

[h2]Requirements[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]RimWorld 1.6[/b].
[*]An agentic AI client with support for local (stdio) MCP servers.
[/list]

[b]Tested with:[/b] Codex & OpenCode.

[h2]Setup[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Enable Rim-MCP in your mod list and restart the game.
[*]Go to Options > Mod settings > Rim-MCP and click [b]Copy MCP config[/b].
[*]Add that config to your client's MCP settings, (Or paste the config to your agent and tell it to configure itself, who has time to edit tomls nowadays).
[*]Turn on RimWorld's [b]Run in background[/b] option so requests work while you're alt-tabbed.
[/olist]

[b]Allow colony changes[/b] is on by default. Turn it off in mod settings for read-only access.

If your client uses a cloud model, it may send colony data to that provider. Your colony data could help shape the mind of future LLMs, what could possibly go wrong?

